.Dd November 9, 2026
.Dt PYDOC3.13 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm pydoc3.13
.Nd the Python documentation tool
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Ss "SYNOPSIS"
.Bd -literal
     pydoc3.13 name

     pydoc3.13 -k keyword

     pydoc3.13 -p port

     pydoc3.13 -g

     pydoc3.13 -w module [...]
.Ed
.Ss "DESCRIPTION"
.Bd -literal
     pydoc3.13 name Show text documentation on something.  name may be the
     name of a Python keyword, topic, function, module, or package, or a
     dotted reference to a class or function within a module or module in a
     package.  If name contains a '/', it is used as the path to a Python
     source file to document. If name is 'keywords', 'topics', or 'modules', a
     listing of these things is displayed.

     pydoc3.13 -k keyword Search for a keyword in the synopsis lines of all
     available modules.

     pydoc3.13 -p port Start an HTTP server on the given port on the local
     machine.

     pydoc3.13 -g Pop up a graphical interface for finding and serving
     documentation.

     pydoc3.13 -w name [...] Write out the HTML documentation for a module to
     a file in the current directory.  If name contains a '/', it is treated
     as a filename; if it names a directory, documentation is written for all
     the contents.
.Ed
.Ss "AUTHOR"
.Bd -literal
     Moshe Zadka, based on "pydoc --help"
.Ed
.Sh RACH2
